    {
      "id": "mt9wwu7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONSTITUTIONAL BODIES OF INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their authority, powers, and duties directly from the Constitution of India.",
        "The UPSC conducts examinations for appointments to All India Services and Central Public Services.",
        "The Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) acts as the guardian of the public purse and audits all expenditure from the Consolidated Fund of India.",
        "The Finance Commission is constituted every 5 years to recommend the distribution of net tax proceeds between the Centre and States.",
        "The Attorney General of India is the highest law officer in the country, appointed by the President under Article 76."
      ],
      "id": "hdyy3q7"
    },
